// INTEL'S CYCLONE 10 GX 10CX085, FROM INTEL'S OWN DOCUMENTS, READ DIRECTLY ON 2026-11-13 at
// docs.altera.com, where Intel's FPGA documentation now lives (the intel.com pages first cited here
// redirect to a not-found page): the Cyclone 10 GX Core Fabric and General Purpose I/Os Handbook
// (document 683775, version 2026.04.28) and the Cyclone 10 GX Device Family Pin Connection Guidelines
// (document 683417, published 2021.10.29). The first reading, on 2026-10-21, went through a search
// index's excerpts and owed this direct read. The direct read corrects it: the handbook's table of
// configuration schemes (Table 69) lists JTAG, active serial x1 and x4 through an EPCQ-L device, passive
// serial and fast passive parallel x8, x16 and x32 "through CPLD or external microcontroller", and
// configuration via protocol over PCIe x1, x2 and x4. Avalon streaming, which the first reading carried,
// is not one of them, and passive serial, fast passive parallel and configuration via protocol were
// missing.
//
// WHAT IS CARRIED, AND FROM WHERE. The schemes (Table 69). The mode-select straps (Table 71, "MSEL Pin
// Settings for Each Configuration Scheme"): MSEL[2..0] 010 and 011 select active serial x1 and x4 at a
// 1.8 V VCCPGM with the fast and the standard power-on reset; 000 and 001 select passive serial and fast
// passive parallel at 1.2, 1.5 or 1.8 V, fast and standard; "JTAG-based configuration" uses "any valid
// MSEL pin settings below", so JTAG is selected by no setting of its own. The guidelines (Table 2):
// "MSEL[0:2] ... These pins are internally connected through a 25-kΩ resistor to GND"; nIO_PULLUP
// "determines the internal pull-ups on user I/O pins and dual-purpose I/O pins ... are on or off before
// and during configuration. A logic high turns off the weak pull-up, while a logic low turns on the weak
// pull-up", with "an internal 25-kΩ pull-down". The configuration signals: "CONF_DONE pin is
// high—indicates that configuration was successful" (JTAG single-device configuration), INIT_DONE,
// optional, reports user mode, and nSTATUS and CONF_DONE go low while nCONFIG is held low (Configuration
// Sequence). The device datasheet's recommended operating conditions (683828, read 2026-10-21 through a
// review's citation of it, not re-read here) make VCCBAT a supply the power-on reset monitors even when no
// volatile key is used; that is por_monitored_supplies, and it is no longer also a vendor statement,
// which the row keeps for the vendor's own sentences verbatim.
//
// WHAT A BOUNDARY SCAN OF IT READS (chapter 9). "You can issue BYPASS, IDCODE, and SAMPLE JTAG
// instructions before, after, or during configuration without having to interrupt configuration"
// (Performing BST). "The SAMPLE JTAG instruction is not supported for high-speed serial interface (HSSI)
// pins" (Table 90, note 29), the transceivers' transmitters, receivers and reference-clock inputs, whose
// boundary cells are IEEE Std 1149.6's (section 9.7): cyclone_10_gx_sample_coverage. "You can perform
// JTAG BST only when both nCONFIG and nSTATUS goes high after power-up" (Performing BST), and "If the
// device is in a reset state and the nCONFIG or nSTATUS signal is low, the device IDCODE might not be
// read correctly" (Table 90's note): cyclone_10_gx_boundary_scan_needs_high. Two documents disagree on
// which instructions exist: the handbook's Table 90 names PULSE_NCONFIG (00 0000 0001, "Emulates pulsing
// the nCONFIG pin low to trigger reconfiguration") and SHIFT_EDERROR_REG, which Intel's description file
// for the device does not list, and the file lists CONFIG_IO, which the table does not. Nothing here sends
// any of the three (product.p4261.j68_scan admits instructions by name from the description file and by
// a closed list of steps).
//
// THE PART. The ordering code 10CX085YF672E6G reads by Intel's code convention as family 10CX (Cyclone
// 10 GX), member 085 (85,000 logic elements, a distributor figure for the same member on 2026-10-21),
// package F (FineLine BGA) with 672 pins, temperature grade E (extended), speed grade 6, G (RoHS); the
// field Y is not decoded here and is owed to the device overview (document 683485). Supply rails and ball
// positions are not carried; the balls are the boundary-scan description's
// (extdeps.electronic_component.intel_10cx085f672_boundary_scan). The mode-select table and the
// boundary-scan statements are the family's, carried with this member because it is the one fitted.
data extdeps_external_authority_anchor: ExternalAuthority = ExternalAuthority {
  uri: Uri {
    scheme: Https
    locator: "docs.altera.com/r/docs/683775/current/cyclone-10-gx-core-fabric-and-general-purpose-i/os-handbook/configuration-sequence"
  }
}

